  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The sole completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yielded a very weak validation accuracy of 0.485 (F1 0.464), barely above chance, suggesting the PCA-based RNA representation alone is insufficient. The most critical open question before investing the remaining 8 experiments in multimodal or more complex configurations is whether the image modality provides a meaningfully stronger signal. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image modality with a standard, well-validated encoder and a simple single-profile setup, directly testing whether visual features carry discriminative information for this task. If image-only accuracy is substantially higher, multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction; if it is similarly weak, the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., encoder quality, task difficulty) and I should pivot toward stronger encoders (scgpt, ViT-L) or multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design choice—modality value—before committing budget to more complex combinations."
}

